This is a classic river crossing puzzle. Here's the solution:

## Solution: 7 Moves

| Move | Action | Left Bank | Right Bank | Status |
|------|--------|-----------|-----------|--------|
| Start | — | Farmer, Fox, Goose, Grain | — | — |
| 1 | Take goose → | Fox, Grain | Farmer, Goose | ✓ Safe (fox & grain ok together) |
| 2 | Return alone ← | Farmer, Fox, Grain | Goose | ✓ Safe (goose alone) |
| 3 | Take fox → | Grain | Farmer, Fox, Goose | ✓ Safe (farmer present) |
| 4 | **Bring goose back ←** | Farmer, Goose, Grain | Fox | ✓ Key step! (prevents fox-goose danger) |
| 5 | Take grain → | Goose | Farmer, Fox, Grain | ✓ Safe (fox & grain ok together) |
| 6 | Return alone ← | Farmer, Goose | Fox, Grain | ✓ Safe (fox & grain ok together) |
| 7 | Take goose → | — | Farmer, Fox, Goose, Grain | ✓ **GOAL!** |

## Key Insight

The critical step is **Move 4**: bringing the goose *back* across the river. This prevents the impossible situation where the fox and goose would be left alone together. By temporarily returning the goose to the left bank, you can safely transport the grain, then return to pick up the goose for the final crossing.

